If the supplier will send the original goods later, their value remains outstanding until delivery. If you agree to apply it to another purchase, it becomes a **supplier credit applied once to that purchase**, not an assumed cash refund.

**Refunding your resellers is separate.** Cancel their affected preorders and refund their actual deposits; that does not clear what the supplier owes you. Because the cancellation is caused by unavailable goods, the customer deposit should not become forfeiture income.

